    "body": "An important difference between the other bits of state you mention is that loop is a content attribute, which means that it should be possible to observe changes with MutationObserver:\r\n```JavaScript\r\nconst video = document.querySelector('video');\r\nnew MutationObserver(() => {\r\n  console.log('loop changed: ' + video.loop)\r\n}).observe(video, {\r\n  attributeFilter: ['loop']\r\n});\r\nvideo.loop = true;\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs that sufficient?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
