    "body": "@foolip hmm, this is interesting! I would say that certainly does appear to supply the desired functionality.\r\n\r\nBut that said, I would argue it might still be worth it to implement a normal DOM event, especially since it appears to be a relatively trivial implementation. `muted` and `volume` are also content attributes, which have an associated DOM event, yes? For consistency's sake, it would be useful. It's much more straightforward to write a series of DOM event listeners for property changes, than a series of DOM event listeners, plus one mutation observer, for the standout property/content attribute which wasn't given a DOM event.",
