    "body": "A content attribute is https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-attribute, i.e. the things that exist on elements, can be seen in markup and set with `element.setAttribute(name, value)`, among other APIs. IDL attributes are https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#idl-attributes and the things that appear in IDL blocks in specs.\r\n\r\nThe list on MDN has a mix of content attributes and IDL attributes, and many are both. However, at least buffered, played, and volume are IDL attributes only. In other words, `<audio volume=\"0.5\">` doesn't work, and an HTML markup validator would complain about it.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
